1. PURPOSE
============================================================

This License establishes:

(a) file-level copyleft for Covered Files;
(b) network-use source disclosure for Covered Software;
(c) cryptographic execution authorization through a Node Key;
(d) preservation of provenance, attribution, and license notices; and
(e) automatic termination upon material breach, subject to applicable law.

This is an independent license.

It is inspired structurally by file-level copyleft concepts associated
with the Mozilla Public License and network-source concepts associated
with the GNU Affero General Public License, but it is NOT the Mozilla
Public License and is NOT the GNU Affero General Public License.

============================================================
2. DEFINITIONS
============================================================

"Covered Software" means any Source Code Form to which this License
has been applied, together with Covered Modifications.

"Covered File" means:

(a) an original source file distributed under this License;

(b) any source file created by modifying, adding to, deleting from,
or incorporating material from a Covered File; and

(c) any new source file containing Covered Software.

"Larger Work" means a work that combines Covered Software with
independent material contained in separate files.

"Modification" means any addition, deletion, transformation,
adaptation, translation, or other change to a Covered File.

"Source Code Form" means the preferred form for making modifications.

"Executable Form" means any form other than Source Code Form.

"Network Service" means making any substantial functionality of the
Covered Software available to a third party through a computer network,
remote interface, hosted service, API, distributed protocol, agent
system, inference endpoint, orchestration service, or similar mechanism.

"Corresponding Service Source" means all source code and associated
materials reasonably necessary to build, install, run, modify, and
operate the version of the Covered Software used to provide the
Network Service.

"Node Key" means a cryptographically verifiable authorization artifact
issued or expressly authorized by the Licensor.

"Node Verification Mechanism" means the software, cryptographic
material, protocol, trust anchor, or verification logic used to
validate a Node Key.

