============================================================
4. FILE-LEVEL COPYLEFT
============================================================

4.1 Covered Files

Every Covered File that You distribute in Source Code Form MUST remain
licensed under this License.

4.2 Modified Files

If You modify a Covered File, that modified file MUST remain available
under this License.

4.3 Larger Works

You may combine Covered Software with independent material in separate
files and distribute the resulting Larger Work under terms of Your
choice for those independent files.

However:

(a) Covered Files remain governed by this License;

(b) You may not impose terms that prevent recipients from exercising
rights granted by this License with respect to Covered Files; and

(c) the requirements of Sections 5 and 6 remain applicable where their
conditions are triggered.

4.4 Source Availability

When distributing Covered Software in Executable Form, You MUST make
the corresponding Source Code Form of Covered Files available by
reasonable means.

============================================================
5. NETWORK-SERVICE SOURCE OBLIGATION
============================================================

5.1 Network Trigger

If You modify Covered Software and make functionality of that modified
Covered Software available to third parties through a Network Service,
You MUST provide those users a clear and reasonably accessible means
to obtain the Corresponding Service Source for the Covered Software
used to provide that service.

5.2 Scope

Corresponding Service Source MUST include, to the extent necessary to
operate the modified Covered Software:

(a) Covered Files;

(b) modifications to Covered Files;

(c) build scripts;

(d) configuration necessary to build and operate the Covered Software;

(e) interface definitions required for the Covered Software to perform
its network-service function; and

(f) source for service-side modifications that form a derivative portion
of the Covered Software.

5.3 Independent Components

Independent programs communicating with Covered Software solely through
ordinary, documented interfaces are not automatically Covered Files
merely because communication occurs across process or network
boundaries.

============================================================
6. CRYPTOGRAPHIC EXECUTION AUTHORIZATION
============================================================

6.1 Mandatory Authorization

Execution of Covered Software, or execution of a Larger Work to the
extent such execution invokes Covered Software, requires a valid
Node Key where the Licensor has designated that release as
"Node-Key Required."

A Node-Key requirement MUST be clearly disclosed in the applicable
release, file notice, manifest, or license metadata.

6.2 Node Verification Mechanism

You may inspect and modify Source Code Form as otherwise permitted by
this License.

However, exercising rights granted by this License does not grant a
right to defeat an applicable Node-Key requirement.

6.3 Prohibited Circumvention

Where a release is designated Node-Key Required, You may not knowingly:

(a) disable the Node Verification Mechanism for the purpose of executing
the Covered Software without authorization;

(b) falsify or spoof a Node Key;

(c) alter verification results for the purpose of bypassing required
authorization;

(d) distribute a patch, key generator, spoofing mechanism, or other
tool whose principal purpose is defeating the Node-Key requirement; or

(e) represent an unauthorized node as an authorized node.

6.4 Security Research

Good-faith security research, interoperability analysis, vulnerability
testing, cryptographic review, and inspection are not prohibited merely
because they analyze or expose weaknesses in the Node Verification
Mechanism, provided such activity does not itself constitute
unauthorized operational use under this License.

6.5 Larger Works

The Node-Key condition applies only to execution of the Covered Software
and functionality dependent upon it.

Nothing in this License automatically converts independent files of a
Larger Work into Covered Files solely because those files are combined
with Covered Software.

============================================================
7. CRYPTOGRAPHIC BINDING
============================================================

The Licensor may implement Node authorization using one or more of:

(a) Ed25519 or equivalent digital signatures;

(b) signed authorization payloads;

(c) hardware-backed device identity;

(d) TPM-backed attestations;

(e) machine or deployment identifiers;

(f) encrypted runtime state;

(g) protected configuration;

(h) signed genesis state;

(i) peer-authentication credentials;

(j) trust-anchor verification; or

(k) protocol-level authorization.

The implementation method does not expand the copyright grant or create
rights beyond those expressly stated in this License.

============================================================
8. NETWORK PEER AUTHENTICATION
============================================================

Covered Software MAY require authenticated peers to present:

(a) a valid Node Key;

(b) a valid cryptographic identity;

(c) a valid protocol certificate; or

(d) another Licensor-approved authorization artifact.

Authorized peers MAY reject network connections from nodes that cannot
satisfy published authentication requirements.

