10. NO SECRET CONVERSION OF COVERED FILES
============================================================

You may not remove a Covered File from the scope of this License merely
by:

(a) renaming it;

(b) translating it;

(c) changing formatting;

(d) moving it into another directory;

(e) changing programming languages while preserving protectable
expression; or

(f) embedding substantially the same Covered Software into another file.

Whether a particular adaptation constitutes a derivative work remains
subject to applicable copyright law.

============================================================
11. TERMINATION
============================================================

11.1 Material Breach

A material failure to comply with Sections 4, 5, 6, or 9 may terminate
the rights granted under this License.

11.2 Automatic Termination

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, rights granted under
this License terminate automatically upon a material breach that remains
uncured.

11.3 Cure

Unless the Licensor provides different written terms, a first-time
violator who completely ceases the violation within thirty (30) days
after receiving written notice may have rights reinstated by written
confirmation from the Licensor.

11.4 No Adjudication by License Text

A statement that conduct violates this License does not by itself
establish civil or criminal liability. Liability and remedies are
determined under applicable law.

